Lesson Set 05 — Audio, Sound Awareness & Character Response
Listening + Playback Path for an R2-Style Droid
Course Introduction Document • DroidWorks U.S.A.
1. Purpose of This Lesson Set
Earlier lesson sets give the droid the ability to notice movement, measure distance, and understand its
own orientation and impacts. Those capabilities answer “what is happening around me and to me?”
Lesson Set 05 adds the voice of the character. It answers two complementary questions:
• Can the droid hear something worth reacting to? (sound awareness)
• Can the droid express itself with sound in response to sensor events? (character playback)
For an R2-style platform this is high-value. Sound is one of the fastest ways to make a collection of
sensors feel like a living character. It is also excellent teaching and content material — reactions are
immediately visible and audible.
