3. Two Practical Paths (Keep Them Modular)
Path A — Simple triggered character sounds (recommended starting point)
Use the MP3 Trigger / voice playback module driven by digital pins or simple serial commands from a
Nano. Sensor events (shock, tilt, motion, later sound detection) select different sound banks. This path
is fast to bring up, easy to teach, and immediately produces character.
Path B — I2S amplified output (MAX98357)
The MAX98357 is an I2S Class-D amplifier. It pairs most cleanly with an ESP32 (or ESP32-S3) rather
than a classic Nano. Use this path when you want higher-quality continuous audio, streaming, or more
advanced synthesis later. It is powerful but introduces a different MCU and I2S considerations, so it is
best treated as a second stage after the simple trigger path is working.
4. Feasibility & MCU Notes
A classic Arduino Nano is fully capable of driving the MP3 Trigger module and reading a MAX9814 (or
simple electret) via analog threshold or basic energy detection. That combination stays consistent with
the millis-based sketches used in earlier sets.
