7. Prerequisites & Recommended Sequence
Audio is deliberately placed after the core sensing layers so that reactions have solid events to respond
to.
Recommended order:
1. Stabilize Lesson Sets 01–03 (motion, ranging, sensor arrays).
2. Complete Lesson Set 04 (orientation, shock, tilt) so discrete “bump” and attitude events exist.
3. Then begin Lesson Set 05 (this audio work), starting with the simple MP3 Trigger path before
adding the MAX98357 I2S path.
This order keeps each layer teachable and prevents audio from becoming a distraction while the
awareness sensors are still being refined.
8. Learning Outcomes
By the end of Lesson Set 05 a student should be able to:
